                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1111 Nelson, Bert N./67: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-03-11T11:00:00+08:00">March 11, 1931—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 11—9:10 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Referring to Hankow’s March 9, 3 p.m., repeated by the Legation, following
                    telegram has been sent American Consul General at Hankow: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“March 10, midnight. I have just seen [Foreign?] Minister who is
                            telegraphing authorities once more to use all means to effect release
                            [of] Nelson and Tvedt and assist those working for their release. Tell
                            Skinsnes to go ahead.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
